# The product is written in the inner loop, and no turn of it changes a factor: it is made once in front of that loop and asked there for an int32, so the key is an integer. In front of that: operations 112 and 15: a test of the width, the product and a key that is a double in every turn.
# When the bound was taken: loop: operations 81, patches 0, moves 0, unlikely 6 ; loop: operations 12, patches 1, moves 0, unlikely 0.
# RUN(X64): loops most:81,12 f1 mechanisms=all-Inlining
# REQUIRES(X64): x86_64 not-windows unsanitized-code faulting-loop-polls as-written
# X64-LABEL: unit f1:Body
# X64-NEXT: loop: at most 81
# X64-NEXT: loop: at most 12
